IMPORT prelude
-- EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC, phase 2 (the run time): the FORK.
--
-- `UPON EACH` fires its HENCE once per member who acts, independently, with
-- the member variable bound to that member (spec §3.2). Three tenants who pay
-- earn three receipts, not one; and a LEST written under a fork blames the
-- member it belongs to, not the group.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord HAS name IS A STRING
    Tenant   HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Pay     HAS payer  IS AN Actor, payee IS AN Actor, amount IS A NUMBER
    Receipt HAS issuer IS AN Actor, to    IS AN Actor, amount IS A NUMBER

theLandlord MEANS Landlord OF "Ms Ng"
alice       MEANS Tenant OF "Alice"
bob         MEANS Tenant OF "Bob"

-- The roll deliberately includes the landlord, so that the cast word `Tenant`
-- is doing visible work: it narrows the roll to the two tenants.
everyone MEANS LIST alice, bob, theLandlord

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`receipts` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN everyone
        MUST   Pay (EXACTLY t) (EXACTLY theLandlord) amount
        WITHIN 7
        UPON   EACH
        HENCE  (PARTY theLandlord
                    MUST   Receipt (EXACTLY theLandlord) (EXACTLY t) (EXACTLY amount)
                    WITHIN 5)
        LEST   BREACH BY t

-- Both tenants pay and both are receipted. `amount`, bound by the action
-- pattern, reaches the receipt: a receipt for the wrong sum would not match.
#TRACE `receipts` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Pay alice theLandlord 100 AT 1
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Receipt theLandlord alice 100 AT 2
  PARTY bob   DOES Pay bob   theLandlord 200 AT 3
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Receipt theLandlord bob 200 AT 4

-- Alice pays and is not receipted. Her fork is still open while Bob's has
-- closed, which is what "independently" means.
#TRACE `receipts` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Pay alice theLandlord 100 AT 1
  PARTY bob   DOES Pay bob   theLandlord 200 AT 3
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Receipt theLandlord bob 200 AT 4

-- Bob never pays. His LEST fires and names him: `t` is bound to the member.
#TRACE `receipts` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Pay alice theLandlord 100 AT 1
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Receipt theLandlord alice 100 AT 2
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Receipt theLandlord bob 200 AT 20
